---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Crt from '../components/Crt.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import { APP, DOWNLOAD, SIGNER, REPO } from '../lib/site';

const verify = `$ codesign -dv --verbose=2 /Applications/ipnx.app
Authority=${SIGNER.authority}
Authority=Developer ID Certification Authority
Authority=Apple Root CA
TeamIdentifier=${SIGNER.teamID}

$ spctl --assess --type execute --verbose /Applications/ipnx.app
/Applications/ipnx.app: accepted
source=Notarized Developer ID`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Download ipnx for Mac"
  description="Download ipnx — Research Unix Eighth Edition on an emulated VAX-11/780 for macOS. Free, signed with a Developer ID and notarised by Apple."
  eyebrow="Distribution"
  heading="Download"
  intro={`${APP.name} ${APP.version} for ${APP.minOS}. Free, and required to be.`}
  appSchema
>
  <div class="grid gap-12 py-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem] lg:items-start">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        The download is a disk image containing one application. Drag it to
        <strong>Applications</strong> and open it; there is no installer, no helper tool, and
        nothing running when the app is not.
      </p>

      <p>
        On first launch it copies its system image into
        <code>~/Library/Application Support/ipnx/v8</code>, creates an account on the emulated
        machine named after your macOS short user name, and logs you in. That takes about half a
        minute. Afterwards it resumes from a snapshot and is ready almost immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>What you are downloading</h2>
      <p>
        Around twenty megabytes, most of it a complete Eighth Edition system — the kernel, the
        commands, the source, the manual and the games. It expands to a 516&nbsp;MB disk on first
        launch, because that is the size of the emulated drive; the compressed form is small
        because a 1985 Unix genuinely was. Nothing is fetched at runtime.
      </p>

      <h2>Signed, and how to check</h2>
      <p>
        The app is signed with a Developer ID certificate and notarised by Apple, so it opens
        without a Gatekeeper warning and without your having to right-click it. You do not have to
        take that on trust — macOS will tell you itself:
      </p>

      <Crt text={verify} caption="Run these against your own copy; the authority line should match exactly." />

      <p>
        <strong>The certificate names a company, and the project does not.</strong> That is
        deliberate and worth explaining rather than hiding. ipnx is a personal, non-commercial
        project, published from a personal account, because the 2017 statement that makes
        Research Unix distributable at all reaches non-commercial use only. A Developer ID
        certificate, however, has to belong to an enrolled Apple developer team, and the one
        available here is <strong>{SIGNER.name}</strong>. So the signature names the team that
        holds the key; the work, the licence position and the responsibility are personal.
      </p>

      <h2>Requirements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>{APP.minOS}</li>
        <li>{APP.architectures} — the VAX and WE32100 cores are built for arm64 only</li>
        <li>About 700&nbsp;MB of disk once the machine has been provisioned</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Not on the App Store yet</h2>
      <p>
        It will be, but not for this edition. The App Store submission waits for Tenth Edition —
        the part of this project that has not been done before — so that what arrives there is the
        restoration rather than the rehearsal. Until then this page is the distribution.
      </p>

      <h2>Source</h2>
      <p>
        Everything is on <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a>: the app, both emulator cores and their
        patches, the V8 source tree, and the build that turns the second into the disk the first
        ships. The <a href={DOWNLOAD.releasesPage}>releases page</a> keeps every version.
      </p>
    </Prose>

    <!-- The download card -->
    <aside class="border border-rule bg-card p-6 lg:sticky lg:top-8">
      <p class="font-sans text-[12px] font-bold tracking-[0.1em] text-muted uppercase">
        Current release
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-serif text-[26px] font-bold">{APP.name} {APP.version}</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">{APP.system}</p>

      <a
        href={DOWNLOAD.url}
        class="mt-5 flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border-2 border-ink bg-ink px-5 py-3 font-sans text-[15px] font-bold text-paper transition hover:bg-transparent hover:text-ink"
      >
        Download {DOWNLOAD.fileName}
      </a>

      <dl class="mt-5 space-y-2 font-sans text-[13px]">
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-3">
          <dt class="text-muted">Requires</dt>
          <dd class="text-right text-ink">{APP.minOS}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-3">
          <dt class="text-muted">Architecture</dt>
          <dd class="text-right text-ink">{APP.architectures}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-3">
          <dt class="text-muted">Price</dt>
          <dd class="text-right text-ink">Free</dd>
        </div>
        {
          DOWNLOAD.size && (
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-3">
              <dt class="text-muted">Size</dt>
              <dd class="text-right text-ink">{DOWNLOAD.size}</dd>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </dl>

      {/*
        The checksum is printed only when there is a real one. An empty or
        placeholder hash is worse than none: it invites a check that cannot
        pass and teaches people to ignore the result.
      */}
      {
        DOWNLOAD.sha256 && (
          <div class="mt-5 border-t border-rule pt-4">
            <p class="font-sans text-[12px] font-bold tracking-[0.1em] text-muted uppercase">
              SHA-256
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] break-all text-body">
              {DOWNLOAD.sha256}
            </p>
          </div>
        )
      }

      <p class="mt-5 border-t border-rule pt-4 font-sans text-[13px] text-muted">
        Signed by {SIGNER.name} ({SIGNER.teamID}) and notarised by Apple.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-sans text-[13px]">
        <a href={DOWNLOAD.releasesPage} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emphasis">
          All releases and notes ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
